[
    {
        "content": "<p>I noticed that some of the lemmas are called Int.divisorsAntidiagonal and others are Int.divisorsAntidiag :(</p>",
        "id": 588744768,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776816335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We should unify the names of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Int.divisorsAntidiag#doc\">docs#Int.divisorsAntidiag</a></p>",
        "id": 588745562,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776816491
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably there's a poll somewhere</p>",
        "id": 588745589,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776816495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/21912\">#21912</a> introduced the short <code>Int</code> version, the long <code>Nat</code> version is from mathlib3 (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/pull/4310\">!3#4310</a>)</p>",
        "id": 588752304,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776818265
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.divisorsAntidiagonalList#doc\">docs#Nat.divisorsAntidiagonalList</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Nat.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#List.Nat.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Multiset.Nat.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Multiset.Nat.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Multiset.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Multiset.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Set.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.HasAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.HasAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.HasMulAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.HasMulAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Nat.antidiagonalTuple#doc\">docs#List.Nat.antidiagonalTuple</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Multiset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple#doc\">docs#Multiset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple#doc\">docs#Finset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.finAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.finAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.mulAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.mulAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.piAntidiag#doc\">docs#Finset.piAntidiag</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.finsuppAntidiag#doc\">docs#Finset.finsuppAntidiag</a></p>\n<p>Well we're definitely not consistent, but it looks like the long version is winning so far (12 vs 3)<br>\n(the two <code>Finset</code> short versions were added in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/13683\">#13683</a>)</p>",
        "id": 588753028,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776818760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> any opinions on this?</p>",
        "id": 590160250,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776851635
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>6 messages were moved here from <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Computable.20.60Fintype.20.7Ba.20.3A.20.E2.84.95.20.2F.2F.20a.20.E2.88.A3.20n.7D.60.20for.20.60fin_cases.60\">#Is there code for X? &gt; Computable &#96;Fintype {a : ℕ // a ∣ n}&#96; for &#96;fin_cases&#96;</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span>.</p>",
        "id": 590234618,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1776869985
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"387244\">Yaël Dillies</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Integer.20Divisors.3F/near/532545587\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The plan here is to rename <code>divisorsAntidiagonal</code> to <code>divisorsAntidiag</code>. I was waiting on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/21915\">#21915</a> to be done before doing so, but I think it's not going to be ready anytime soon, so feel free to rename <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal</a> now!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 590234841,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776870030
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>btw, what about <code>diag</code> vs <code>diagonal</code>? <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.diagonal#doc\">docs#Set.diagonal</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.offDiag#doc\">docs#Set.offDiag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.offDiag#doc\">docs#List.offDiag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.offDiag#doc\">docs#Finset.offDiag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sym2.diagSet#doc\">docs#Sym2.diagSet</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diag#doc\">docs#Matrix.diag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diagonal#doc\">docs#Matrix.diagonal</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38380\">#38380</a></p>",
        "id": 590312504,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776895993
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm strongly in favor of the long version, which is easier to discover and to read.</p>",
        "id": 592692217,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1777887908
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Strangely I prefer <code>antidiagonal</code> to <code>antidiag</code>, but <code>diag</code> to <code>diagonal</code> (at least sometimes).<br>\nSpecifically I think <code>Matrix.diag</code> is nice. We like <code>rfl</code>/<code>refl</code>/<code>symm</code>/<code>trans</code>/<code>mono</code>/<code>comp</code>/<code>re</code>/<code>im</code>/<code>hom</code>/<code>iso</code>/<code>equiv</code>/<code>congr</code>/<code>coe</code>/<code>eq</code>/<code>ne</code>/<code>le</code>/<code>prod</code>/<code>mul</code>/<code>pow</code>, so why not <code>diag</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592702575,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777891334
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OTOH I think <code>Matrix.toLin</code> should be <code>Matrix.toLinearMap</code> (<span aria-label=\"hot pepper\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f336\" role=\"img\" title=\"hot pepper\">:hot_pepper:</span>)</p>",
        "id": 592702631,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777891351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that we have both <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diag#doc\">docs#Matrix.diag</a> and also <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diagonal#doc\">docs#Matrix.diagonal</a>, which compose to the identity</p>",
        "id": 592704832,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777892022
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that the first should be <code>Matrix.diagonal</code> and the second, <code>Matrix.ofDiagonal</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592705580,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1777892254
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A more cursed option would be to copy numpy and have a single name for both functions, via a type class to do the dispatch</p>",
        "id": 593579084,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778173612
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/stream/287929-mathlib4/topic/antidiagonal.20vs.20antidiag/near/592705580\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think that the first should be <code>Matrix.diagonal</code> and the second, <code>Matrix.ofDiagonal</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This has the downside of giving the far more useful operation the longer name</p>",
        "id": 593579342,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778173685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, that would be very cursed.</p>",
        "id": 593584615,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1778175137
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that long names strike back when you need something like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousMultilinearMap.compContinuousLinearMapL#doc\">docs#ContinuousMultilinearMap.compContinuousLinearMapL</a> where the trailing <code>L</code> should probably be replaced by something like <code>AsContinuousLinearMap</code>, if we go for long names.</p>",
        "id": 593588585,
        "sender_full_name": "Yury G. Kudryashov",
        "timestamp": 1778176240
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think my <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38380\">#38380</a> is going to want to wait for this to be fixed, because trying to do a PR on top or in paralell is going to be a mare.</p>",
        "id": 620655891,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1788268276
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have any consensus on exactly the rename schema?</p>",
        "id": 620656365,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1788268351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38380\">#38380</a> would have added Set.diag, matching Finset.diag, but I've been told given we're changing names it can't now merge. But Set.diagonal exists...)</p>",
        "id": 620656844,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1788268425
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What to do about Matrix.diag and Matrix.diagonal I don't know. But I really feel like things have been thrown into uncertainty now for me.</p>",
        "id": 620657531,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1788268551
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"933054\">@Snir Broshi</span> re: github</p>",
        "id": 620676278,
        "sender_full_name": "Wrenna Robson",
        "timestamp": 1788271897
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"330967\">Wrenna Robson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/antidiagonal.20vs.20antidiag/near/620655891\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think my <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38380\">#38380</a> is going to want to wait for this to be fixed</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I don't think anyone is working on this, so waiting might take a while.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"330967\">Wrenna Robson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/antidiagonal.20vs.20antidiag/near/620657531\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I really feel like things have been thrown into uncertainty now for me.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>My point was to draw your attention to this thread; I don't understand how that lead to this.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"330967\">Wrenna Robson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/antidiagonal.20vs.20antidiag/near/620656844\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I've been told given we're changing names it can't now merge.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I never said such a thing, and I even clarified I hold no authority.</p>",
        "id": 620877493,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788324021
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I like the idea of renaming <code>Set.diagonal</code> to <code>Prod.diagonalSet</code>; I prefer it over <code>Set.diagonalUniv</code>.</p>\n<p>Then we could have:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">diagonal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">diagonal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">diagonalSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(these are currently <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Function.diag#doc\">docs#Function.diag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.prod#doc\">docs#Set.prod</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38380\">#38380</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.diagonal#doc\">docs#Set.diagonal</a>)<br>\nand</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">diagonal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sym2Diagonal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsDiag</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">diagonalSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sym2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsDiag</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(these are currently <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sym2.diag#doc\">docs#Sym2.diag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.sym2#doc\">docs#Set.sym2</a>, N/A, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sym2.diagSet#doc\">docs#Sym2.diagSet</a>)</p>",
